    body: ['For two dice, draw a 6-by-6 grid and fill it with the SUM (or the PRODUCT, or the difference) of the two faces. Then count cells.', 'SUMS run from 2 (1+1) to 12 (6+6). The most likely sum is 7 (six cells: 1+6, 2+5, 3+4, 4+3, 5+2, 6+1). The least likely sums are 2 and 12 (one cell each).', 'PRODUCTS go from 1 to 36 — but the same product can appear in many cells, and many products in 1–36 do NOT appear at all.', 'Tip: when the question asks for "less than 5", count cells with sum 2, 3, or 4 — it is easy to forget the boundary.'],
